WEBVTT

00:09:59.405 --> 00:10:01.476
the year he won the Nobel Prize.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.903
I'd be willing to bet
that we would either uncover,

00:10:03.927 --> 00:10:07.744
or even create more Frank Lloyd Wrights
and more Raymond Davises

00:10:07.768 --> 00:10:10.696
if we had ways of keeping
more people motivated to produce

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.540
into and past mid career.

00:10:12.907 --> 00:10:14.312
Agree or disagree?

00:10:15.329 --> 00:10:16.519
AB: I think

00:10:16.543 --> 00:10:21.185
that if there is a natural cadence
to the average person's life,

00:10:21.209 --> 00:10:23.550
and you're saying
it doesn't have to be this way,

00:10:23.574 --> 00:10:26.518
then the societal goal
will be one in which

00:10:26.542 --> 00:10:28.300
everybody is above average.

00:10:28.324 --> 00:10:32.429
And you know, that becomes
an exercise in frustration.